{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 7.767,
   "text": "I work nights in the last toll booth before the mountain pass."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 8.367,
   "end": 13.167,
   "text": "The old collector, Gus, left me one rule, taped above the coin tray."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 13.767,
   "end": 19.164,
   "text": "If anyone pays with a silver dollar... lift the gate. And don't look inside the car."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 20.164,
   "end": 24.815,
   "text": "For a month, it was only truckers, fog, and the hum of my little heater."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 25.515,
   "end": 30.827,
   "text": "Then, at three a.m., a long gray station wagon rolled up. Headlights off."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 32.027,
   "end": 37.787,
   "text": "The window cranked down. A hand, white as frost, dropped a silver dollar in my tray."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 38.387,
   "end": 39.191,
   "text": "Clink."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 40.591,
   "end": 44.218,
   "text": "I kept my eyes on the coin. I lifted the gate."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 45.018,
   "end": 49.007,
   "text": "But as it rolled past... I glanced at the back windows."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 50.007,
   "end": 55.02,
   "text": "Faces. Pale and still. Every one of them pressed to the glass... watching me."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 56.22,
   "end": 61.212,
   "text": "And in the last seat, I saw Gus. The man who quit without saying goodbye."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 63.412,
   "end": 67.892,
   "text": "Last night, that wagon came back... and Gus was the one driving."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 69.292,
   "end": 73.09,
   "text": "He opened the back door... and patted the empty seat."
  }
 ],
